      "body": "## Review Summary\n\nI reviewed the diff between `main` (a7eb18b7) and the PR head (d1f5972), covering the new `FetchPRReviewThreads` GraphQL fetch and `PRReviewThread`/`PRReviewThreadComment` types in `github/`, the prompt-assembly changes (`renderReviewThreads`, `selectPromptThreads`, the R2/R5 wording) and `ReviewThreads` plumbing in `pruefer/claude.go`/`review.go`, and the new `dedupeFindings` in `pruefer/findings.go`. The change is well tested (boundary cases for the 20-thread cap, null-line fallback, comment truncation, severity-collision dedup, non-vacuous prompt-inclusion tests) and the accompanying ADR is unusually thorough, including an explicit, reasoned acceptance of the widened prompt-injection surface from interpolating untrusted thread-comment bodies \u2014 so I'm not re-raising that as a new finding since it's already identified and consciously accepted with rationale.\n\n`go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, and `go test ./pruefer/... ./github/...` all pass locally (562 tests).\n\nOne real design gap: `dedupeFindings` collapses any two findings sharing `(Path, Line)` on the assumption they're the same defect restated, but nothing verifies that \u2014 and unlike `partitionFindings` (which happily emits multiple separate inline `ReviewComment`s at the same anchor, since GitHub's review API supports that), this new step will silently discard a genuinely distinct finding that happens to land on the same line as another, with no merge and no trace of what was dropped.",
