      "body": "## Review\n\nI reviewed the full diff for #1505 against `main` (the fetch/thread-context plumbing in `github/prs.go` and `github/types.go`, the prompt-assembly and dedup logic in `pruefer/claude.go`/`pruefer/findings.go`, the `ReviewPR` wiring in `pruefer/review.go`, and the accompanying tests and ADR). The change is well-scoped to the stated goal (R1\u2013R5), the degrade-not-fail behavior for thread-fetch errors is correctly wired and tested, `dedupeFindings`'s merge-not-discard fix (the subject of the most recent commit) is correct and covered by a dedicated collision test, and the `maxPromptThreads` cap/ordering is tested at and over the boundary. `go build`, `go vet`, and `go test ./pruefer/... ./github/...` all pass locally. The ADR is unusually thorough and explicitly documents the widened prompt-injection surface as an accepted, bounded trade-off, so I did not re-raise that as a fresh finding. Only one minor observation surfaced, below.",
