      "body": "I reviewed this PR's core changes: `github.FetchPRReviewThreads` (new GraphQL fetch), `ReviewPR`'s wiring of thread context with non-fatal error degradation, `buildReviewPrompt`/`renderReviewThreads`/`selectPromptThreads`/`truncateCommentBody` in `pruefer/claude.go`, and `dedupeFindings`/`mergeFindings` in `pruefer/findings.go`, along with the corresponding `PRReviewThread` types and tests.\n\nThe implementation is careful and well-documented: the thread fetch is correctly treated as advisory (logged and degraded to `nil` on error, unlike the eligibility-gating `FetchPRReviews`), the prompt-size bound is layered at three levels (thread count, per-thread comment count, per-comment body length) with truncation always surfaced to the reviewer rather than silently dropped, and `dedupeFindings` merges same-anchor findings without discarding content (a safer choice than the PR description's \"keeping the higher-severity entry\" phrasing suggests, but functionally sound \u2014 it concatenates bodies and takes the max severity). Known tradeoffs (e.g., the 20-comment-per-thread GraphQL page missing a later resolving reply, `threadLastCommentTime` only seeing the fetched page) are explicitly acknowledged in comments rather than hidden. Test coverage for the new fetch, cap boundaries, and dedup collision cases looks appropriately targeted per the PR's test plan.\n\nNo bugs, security issues, or design problems found in the reviewed diff surface.",
