      "body": "I reviewed the pruefer prior-thread-context feature: `github.FetchPRReviewThreads` (GraphQL fetch of resolved/unresolved review threads), `pruefer/review.go`'s wiring into `ReviewRequest`, `pruefer/claude.go`'s `renderReviewThreads`/`selectPromptThreads`/`truncateCommentBody` prompt assembly, and `pruefer/findings.go`'s `dedupeFindings`, along with the accompanying ADR. Note: the checked-out repo is a single-commit shallow clone with no `main` ref available locally, so I reviewed the changed subsystem's current-state files directly.\n\nThe implementation is careful and well-tested: thread-fetch failures degrade non-fatally (unlike the fatal `FetchPRReviews` gate), the prompt is bounded on both thread count (`maxPromptThreads`) and per-comment size (`maxThreadCommentBodyChars`), truncation is always surfaced rather than silent, and `dedupeFindings` merges rather than discards on same-anchor collisions (a fix already applied earlier in this PR's history per the commit log). The ADR is unusually candid about trade-offs, including an explicitly accepted prompt-injection surface widening from interpolating untrusted thread-comment bodies into the prompt \u2014 I don't think there's a hidden issue there beyond what's already documented as accepted risk. Two smaller points below.",
